---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getSeasons, references } from '@/lib/seasons';

const seasons = await getSeasons();
const totalEntries = seasons.reduce((sum, season) => sum + season.data.entryCount, 0);
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="How this MU Online timeline is sourced and generated.">
  <div class="page-shell max-w-3xl py-10 sm:py-12">
    <h1 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-ink-100 sm:text-4xl">About this project</h1>

    <div class="season-prose mt-8">
      <p>
        This site documents the release history of <strong>MU Online</strong> — every version,
        season and notable patch from the 2001 closed alpha in South Korea through to the current
        season. It currently covers <strong>{seasons.length} releases</strong>, <strong
          >{totalEntries} individual changes</strong
        > and <strong>{references.length} cited sources</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>Credits</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>
          All of the historical research presented here comes from the <a
            href="https://github.com/AlighieriDemiurgs/MuHistory"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">AlighieriDemiurgs/MuHistory</a
          > repository.
        </strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        Every date, patch note, correction and citation was gathered, verified and cross-referenced
        by the maintainer of that project — including the archival work of tracking down long-dead
        Korean patch pages through the Wayback Machine. Full credit for the content belongs to
        them.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site contributes only the presentation layer. It is an independent project, not
        affiliated with or endorsed by the MuHistory maintainer. For the canonical, actively
        maintained version of the history — and to submit corrections to it — go to <a
          href="https://github.com/AlighieriDemiurgs/MuHistory"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">the source repository</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>Sourcing</h2>
      <p>
        Nearly every entry carries one or more citation numbers. Those link to the <a
          href="/references">references page</a
        >, where each source points at an archived copy of the original patch note, announcement or
        press release — most via the Wayback Machine, since the original Korean pages are long
        gone.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where sources conflict or evidence is thin, the timeline says so directly in a nested note
        under the entry rather than picking a side silently.
      </p>

      <h2>How the site is built</h2>
      <p>
        The whole timeline lives in a single research document, <code>source.md</code>. A build
        script (<code>scripts/split-source.mjs</code>) splits it into one markdown file per season,
        extracts the reference list into JSON, and rewrites the inline citation markup into links.
        Astro then renders those as static pages — no client-side framework, no database.
      </p>
      <p>
        That document is a copy of the upstream MuHistory research, so factual corrections belong
        there rather than here — this site picks them up when it re-syncs and rebuilds.
      </p>

      <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        Community research project, not affiliated with or endorsed by Webzen Inc. MU Online and
        related names are trademarks of their respective owners.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
